1.
API - Application Programming Interface is a set of commands, functions, protocols,
and objects that programmers can use to create software or interact with an
external system.
Eg: We can interact with websites in the internet and pull live data from these websites.

- We use the rules prescribed by the API to make requests to the external system.
- We can use the API website of each target website to know what the rules
of interaction are and to make valid requests to the target website to, say, pull live data.

2.
API ENDPOINTS AND MAKING API CALLS
Analogy - In order to get money from the bank, you need to know where the bank is.
In the same way, in order to get something from the website, api acts as teh bank branch of the
website. API is the bank teller that is a means of access to the vault.

API is usually a url that can be used to connect to the api. That is called an API ENDPOINT.

NOTE: api calls return json data

3.
How to get api data into a python prgram

step1 - import requests to the program
eg: import requests

step2 - make request to get response from an api endpoint (ie. url)
eg :
response = requests.get(url="<put url here>")

if we print response, we will get a number. That is a response code.

Meaning of response codes (like 404) - short summary is to look at the left most digit
1xx = Hold on, process not complete yet
2xx = Here you go, response receive is successful
3xx = You dont have permission to make a request like that
4xx = You made a mistake in the request like mistae in url
5xx = Server made mistake in its processing of the response

We can derive certain information from the response code as well
eg:
status_code - which is to just print the response code value
We can use this attribute to raise different exceptions to different response failures

https://www.webfx.com/web-development/glossary/http-status-codes/
website that describes meaning of each status code

We can also raise tailored exceptions using the methods of requests module

EG: response.raise_for_status()
this would raise exceptions based on unsuccessful error code

STEP 3- to get the json file after getting the response

eg: data = response.json()

We can also get specific values from the json as dictionary subscriptions
eg: data[<key>]


